  "slug": "lipid-composition-c3e1",
  "summary": "New coarse-grained frameworks now cover N-glycoproteins, Histatin 1 self-association and PFKL filaments, extending simulations to larger, more complex assemblies.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is reduced-resolution simulation applied to protein association and assembly at scales beyond routine all-atom MD. GlycoMarinate automates Martini 3 modelling of N-glycoproteins, offering transferable and refined glycan models. For Histatin 1, atomistic and coarse-grained MD combined with trajectory decomposition map a multivalent, aromatic-driven self-association pathway. For human liver PFKL, a shape-based rigid-body model with interface-specific interaction sites simulates filament assembly from tetramers. The items differ in resolution and target: a Martini-based automation tool, a multiscale pathway analysis, and a highly coarse-grained rigid-body model. What is new is the automation and transferability of glycan parameterization, alongside interface-specific coarse-graining used to reconstruct assembly pathways and filament organization.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
